WEBVTT



00:00:32.365 --> 00:00:39.039
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

00:00:39.539 --> 00:00:46.504
5 YEARS AGO, SLOVAKIA

00:00:56.264 --> 00:00:57.098
Brother Luca.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:01.895
How are you feeling today?

00:01:04.481 --> 00:01:05.315
I'm okay.

00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:08.777
Thank you brother, for taking interest
in my well-being.

00:01:09.861 --> 00:01:11.780
This is for you. I was in town earlier

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:14.949
and I heard them say that an Asian
man, like you

00:01:15.033 --> 00:01:16.576
was going to perform tonight.

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:19.329
It might be good for you to see him.
You never know…

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:20.497
it might be what you need.

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.123
I think this will help you

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:23.166
regain

00:01:23.249 --> 00:01:24.250
some of your memory.

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:27.420
Thank you.

00:01:55.031 --> 00:01:55.865
N

00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:01.246
Just like you told me. Freely.

00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:03.206
It's all your fault!

00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:51.713
Kang Pi-o.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:03.516
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

00:03:04.809 --> 00:03:06.561
EPISODE 8

00:03:24.329 --> 00:03:25.997
JAE-IN ARE YOU UP?

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.790
PI-O, I'M SORRY
ARE YOU STILL MAD?

00:03:31.336 --> 00:03:32.170
I'm not.

00:03:32.754 --> 00:03:34.088
I'll call you later, okay?

00:03:34.839 --> 00:03:35.673
SEND

00:03:43.139 --> 00:03:43.973
Listen,

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:47.435
I know he's a genius and what not, but I
think it's a bit ridiculous to bring in

00:03:47.518 --> 00:03:50.313
a twenty-seven-year-old as a conductor
for this orchestra.

00:03:50.396 --> 00:03:52.815
Maestro Kang wouldn't just bring in
anyone.

00:03:53.691 --> 00:03:56.903
Truth be told, I saw him at the Brno
competition and he was good.

00:03:56.986 --> 00:03:57.820
He was good?

00:03:59.155 --> 00:04:00.073
What's he good at?

00:04:00.949 --> 00:04:02.992
Did he do a good job, or was it the
orchestra?

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:04.869
I mean… I guess we'll find out soon.

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:06.246
Hey, Jang Seok-hwan.

00:04:06.871 --> 00:04:09.624
Are you bothered that your classmate
will be the conductor? Are you

00:04:09.707 --> 00:04:10.792
jealous or something?

00:04:11.376 --> 00:04:12.293
I'm not, come on.

00:04:12.794 --> 00:04:16.589
I think we should test him. At measure
eleven, I'll go half a beat faster.

00:04:16.673 --> 00:04:19.801
I'm certain… that he won't know Uh…
why the hell the sound seems off.

00:04:19.884 --> 00:04:21.010
Who would notice that?

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.053
Only Maestro Kang.

00:04:23.012 --> 00:04:23.846
Huh…

00:04:47.787 --> 00:04:49.622
Hello, members of the orchestra.

00:04:49.706 --> 00:04:53.293
As we had previously announced, our new
principal guest conductor, Luca

00:04:53.376 --> 00:04:56.337
Domenico, will be leading all your
rehearsals as of today.

00:04:56.421 --> 00:04:57.547
Now,

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.841
I would like to introduce you to your
Conductor.

00:04:59.924 --> 00:05:00.758
Please come up.

00:05:05.179 --> 00:05:06.055
Hello everybody.

00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:08.016
I'm Luca Domenico, and I…

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:09.350
am honored to be here.

00:05:14.355 --> 00:05:17.442
We know his name is Choi Jeong-yo, why
introduce himself as Luca Dominico?

00:05:17.525 --> 00:05:18.359
It's weird.

00:05:21.362 --> 00:05:22.739
Let me say this in advance.

00:05:23.698 --> 00:05:27.285
If you have any complaints or
suggestions, please talk to me directly.

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:29.203
If not, don't even bother

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:31.581
saying anything then.

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:36.461
The one and only thing we should be
discussing in the rehearsal room is

00:05:36.544 --> 00:05:38.338
music. Are we clear on that?

00:05:38.421 --> 00:05:39.255
Alright, then…

00:05:40.381 --> 00:05:42.967
let's begin from the top of Brahms' first
movement.

00:06:45.613 --> 00:06:46.531
One of the cellists

00:06:46.614 --> 00:06:48.783
is late on the attack in measure eleven.

00:06:50.284 --> 00:06:51.119
Principal Cello?

00:06:53.663 --> 00:06:56.040
Oh. Um, that was totally my mistake.

00:06:56.124 --> 00:06:57.542
I… I'm really sorry about it.

00:06:57.625 --> 00:06:59.377
Uh… But…

00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:01.337
I wasn't late on the attack.

00:07:01.421 --> 00:07:02.255
I was early.

00:07:03.506 --> 00:07:04.340
Well…

00:07:05.049 --> 00:07:07.135
I guess you're not that precise, are you?

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:10.012
-No, you were late.
-I wasn't.

00:07:10.513 --> 00:07:11.514
I was early.

00:07:11.597 --> 00:07:14.976
You are a musician, like the rest of us.
But are you even aware of what a bad

00:07:15.059 --> 00:07:15.893
habit you have?

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:19.564
Other players with the same habit you're
showing,

00:07:20.314 --> 00:07:22.608
tend to drag the opening note
of a phrase.

00:07:22.692 --> 00:07:26.446
So even if your bow moves first, the note
will still come in a beat behind.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:28.531
This habit of yours

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:31.242
causes the sound to repeatedly
come in late.

00:07:32.452 --> 00:07:35.204
The fact that you didn't even notice you
were doing it…

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:38.916
only proves to me that you are severely
out of practice.

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:42.587
And it compromises the sound of the whole
orchestra.

00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:48.426
Just playing the cello doesn't make you
a good musician.

00:07:49.218 --> 00:07:50.136
Put in the effort.

00:07:50.636 --> 00:07:51.471
And practice.

00:07:53.097 --> 00:07:54.932
Start again from the first movement.

00:08:10.156 --> 00:08:10.990
Wow,

00:08:11.073 --> 00:08:13.075
you're more experienced than I expected.

00:08:13.993 --> 00:08:17.997
I knew you had a good ear, but how are
you so good at handling an orchestra too?

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:21.459
Oh… There's someone waiting to see you.

00:08:23.002 --> 00:08:23.920
Waiting to see me?

00:08:24.420 --> 00:08:25.922
Yes, exactly.

00:08:44.732 --> 00:08:45.566
Choi…

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:48.569
Jeong-yo. Do you remember me?

00:08:51.113 --> 00:08:53.241
I… used to teach you piano.

00:08:54.825 --> 00:08:55.785
I'm Do Hyun-soo.

00:09:03.584 --> 00:09:04.669
I'm so sorry, but I…

00:09:05.419 --> 00:09:06.712
-I…
-It's okay.

00:09:09.131 --> 00:09:10.550
Don't you worry about it.

00:09:14.428 --> 00:09:16.305
Would it be okay if I gave you a hug?

00:09:17.890 --> 00:09:18.724
Sure.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:25.314
Hmm…

00:09:29.485 --> 00:09:31.862
I'm sorry that I didn't come to see you
sooner.

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:35.199
You must be having a hard time
settling in here.

00:09:36.033 --> 00:09:38.160
I thought I'd only make things worse,
so I…

00:09:38.244 --> 00:09:39.161
waited to see you.

00:09:42.248 --> 00:09:43.916
You know, after you went missing…

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:48.045
Ms. Yoon and I kept searching for
you for the longest time, but…

00:09:51.507 --> 00:09:53.342
We could've never imagined you'd be…

00:09:53.968 --> 00:09:55.011
at a monastery.

00:09:57.179 --> 00:09:58.347
Why do all that for me?

00:10:00.891 --> 00:10:02.393
You know, you were my student.

00:10:03.019 --> 00:10:03.894
I care about you.

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:06.147
And also, because I was the one

00:10:06.230 --> 00:10:07.356
who sent you there.

00:10:08.232 --> 00:10:11.193
I felt terrible for not trying harder to
talk you out of it

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:13.904
ever since you came to me saying

00:10:14.488 --> 00:10:16.115
that you wanted to compete.

00:10:16.198 --> 00:10:18.659
You were perfectly happy doing music
on your own…

00:10:19.493 --> 00:10:20.870
then I dragged you into it.

00:10:21.996 --> 00:10:23.039
I regret doing that.

00:10:28.419 --> 00:10:29.545
Still, I'm glad to see

00:10:30.212 --> 00:10:31.714
the amazing man you've become.

00:10:32.923 --> 00:10:34.133
I heard you told Ms. Yoon

00:10:34.216 --> 00:10:37.136
that you were thinking of performing
a concerto with Pi-o.

00:10:37.219 --> 00:10:38.054
Oh…

00:10:38.137 --> 00:10:41.307
I saw a video of Mr. Kang Pi-o 's
performance and thought that we

00:10:41.390 --> 00:10:42.642
might work well together.

00:10:45.227 --> 00:10:46.854
You probably don't remember him.

00:10:47.396 --> 00:10:48.230
Was it…

00:10:48.314 --> 00:10:51.025
a coincidence, or did you have a gut
feeling about it?

00:10:51.984 --> 00:10:53.402
Because back in high school,

00:10:54.111 --> 00:10:54.945
Pi-o and you,

00:10:55.029 --> 00:10:57.198
were really quite amazing playing
together.

00:10:58.824 --> 00:11:00.576
I really hope you can convince Pi-o

00:11:01.202 --> 00:11:04.121
and help him regain the confidence
to return to the stage.

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:08.334
Pi-o's been struggling lately. He's been
in a slump for quite a while.

00:11:08.417 --> 00:11:09.752
I'm sure you know that.

00:11:52.169 --> 00:11:53.587
MESSAGES NEW MESSAGE

00:11:59.051 --> 00:12:00.428
CHOI JEONG-YO

00:12:00.511 --> 00:12:01.887
Do you think we could meet?

00:12:06.767 --> 00:12:09.228
Why don't you want to perform a concerto
with me?

00:12:09.729 --> 00:12:12.773
Are you afraid of the stage? Or is
performing with me

00:12:12.857 --> 00:12:14.024
what's uncomfortable.

00:12:15.901 --> 00:12:17.403
To be honest with you,

00:12:17.486 --> 00:12:18.320
it's both.

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:20.489
I'm sure you heard from Jae-in,

00:12:21.073 --> 00:12:21.907
that I've made

00:12:26.328 --> 00:12:27.163
a huge mistake

00:12:27.872 --> 00:12:28.914
on stage recently.

00:12:29.665 --> 00:12:31.542
I still haven't recovered from that.

00:12:32.042 --> 00:12:33.502
I appreciate the opportunity,

00:12:34.462 --> 00:12:36.547
but I think you should find someone else.

00:12:40.926 --> 00:12:43.804
If that's the issue, your decision
doesn't make any sense.

00:12:43.888 --> 00:12:45.806
-What do you mean?
-Think about it.

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:48.142
Well, the problem as I see it…

00:12:48.768 --> 00:12:50.936
is that you can't just run away from
a slump.

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.773
The only way you can get through it
is to face it head-on.

00:12:53.856 --> 00:12:55.024
Do you agree?

00:12:56.108 --> 00:12:59.028
But you can't solve a problem by ignoring
it, you know that.

00:12:59.111 --> 00:13:01.781
It's a hurdle you need to overcome,
sooner or later.

00:13:08.829 --> 00:13:10.080
Thank you for the advice,

00:13:10.581 --> 00:13:11.957
but I can handle it myself.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:13.959
You better find someone else.

00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:22.760
N

00:13:29.266 --> 00:13:30.100
Welcome.

00:13:30.184 --> 00:13:32.061
-I think we should celebrate.
-Table for two.

00:13:32.144 --> 00:13:33.270
Please follow me, sir.

00:13:33.854 --> 00:13:36.065
-Let's cheers to that!
-Are you being serious now?

00:13:36.148 --> 00:13:37.900
-Yes I am!
-Oh, boy, Choi Jeong-yo.

00:13:38.609 --> 00:13:41.070
You've always had a way of throwing
people for a loop.

00:13:41.153 --> 00:13:43.781
Still, you should've told me about it. I
would've.

00:13:44.824 --> 00:13:47.451
I nearly had a heart attack when I saw
the news!

00:13:47.535 --> 00:13:50.412
You didn't need to worry, but I guess
you worried anyway.

00:13:51.789 --> 00:13:53.457
How could I not worry about that?

00:13:54.375 --> 00:13:57.378
You disappeared, never showed your face,
and now you're here.

00:13:57.461 --> 00:13:59.088
How could I know you'd be fine?

00:13:59.839 --> 00:14:00.798
So how's dad?

00:14:00.881 --> 00:14:02.466
Oh… jeez.

00:14:05.761 --> 00:14:07.179
He's absolutely fantastic!

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.975
Every time he sneaks out of the hospital
for a drink, I have to chase him down to

00:14:11.058 --> 00:14:11.892
bring him back.

00:14:11.976 --> 00:14:14.979
Man, I swear, I just don't understand why
you keep wasting your money on

00:14:15.062 --> 00:14:15.896
that deadbeat.

00:14:20.192 --> 00:14:21.443
Hey, by the way, tell me…

00:14:22.152 --> 00:14:23.863
uh, when did you learn to do that?

00:14:28.367 --> 00:14:29.201
You are…

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:31.829
just really good at everything you do.

00:14:33.914 --> 00:14:35.332
If you hadn't been kidnapped,

00:14:35.416 --> 00:14:37.543
you would've crushed that competition
too.

00:14:38.752 --> 00:14:42.381
But hey man, why are you going around
telling people you've got amnesia?

00:14:43.632 --> 00:14:45.843
Why not just expose them and put them
in jail?

00:14:45.926 --> 00:14:49.388
And if that's not enough, we can go
find them and beat them ourselves.

00:14:49.471 --> 00:14:50.306
Got it?

00:14:50.890 --> 00:14:51.724
Hey,

00:14:51.807 --> 00:14:55.019
I could maybe break two… of his fingers?
Or I could just make that bastard

00:14:55.102 --> 00:14:57.229
disappear. I'm good with that.

00:14:57.938 --> 00:14:59.440
Where's the fun in doing that?

00:15:00.232 --> 00:15:01.066
Huh?

00:15:04.820 --> 00:15:06.155
Well, don't you know that…

00:15:08.324 --> 00:15:10.659
the waiting is worse… than the actual
beating?

00:15:15.664 --> 00:15:17.958
N You've planned the whole thing already!

00:15:18.459 --> 00:15:20.169
Come on, man, let me in on it.

00:15:22.546 --> 00:15:23.923
What are you talking about?

00:15:31.555 --> 00:15:34.892
Pi-o and Jeong-yo performing together?
I am absolutely against it.

00:15:35.976 --> 00:15:37.019
Uh, really?

00:15:37.102 --> 00:15:38.187
But why not?

00:15:39.146 --> 00:15:42.316
I get why Pi-o wouldn't want to, but why
are you so against it?

00:15:42.942 --> 00:15:45.027
Look, we haven't said anything to you,

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.655
but everyone knows that Pi-o's in a slump
right now.

00:15:47.738 --> 00:15:49.823
His invitations are drying up, you know?

00:15:49.907 --> 00:15:51.909
He's turned down the few we got so, yeah.

00:15:51.992 --> 00:15:53.118
I'd say it's an issue.

00:15:54.453 --> 00:15:56.956
Do you want to see Pi-o be forgotten
by the world?

00:15:57.039 --> 00:15:58.958
Taking a break won't end his career.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:01.919
Plenty of pianists have done just that.

00:16:02.002 --> 00:16:03.128
Hey…

00:16:03.837 --> 00:16:05.172
You can be honest with me.

00:16:05.881 --> 00:16:07.675
Tell me why you hate this idea.

00:16:07.758 --> 00:16:10.886
Is it because you don't want him being
compared to Jeong-yo?

00:16:10.970 --> 00:16:12.429
Or is there… another reason?

00:16:13.347 --> 00:16:15.766
Who told you they would compare him
to Jeong-yo?

00:16:16.475 --> 00:16:19.812
I'm afraid that if we push him right now,
it'll make things worse.

00:16:19.895 --> 00:16:20.980
Do you…

00:16:21.522 --> 00:16:23.399
just not have any more faith in Pi-o?

00:16:24.483 --> 00:16:27.820
If we just give him some space, he'll get
back on his feet on his own.

00:16:27.903 --> 00:16:30.864
Don't even bother bringing up
the concerto to him again.

00:16:31.615 --> 00:16:34.034
He'll get out of his slump in his own
damn time.

00:16:35.869 --> 00:16:36.704
Oh, jeez…

00:16:37.955 --> 00:16:38.789
Wait.

00:16:39.707 --> 00:16:42.251
Is she seriously still bothered by
Choi Jeong-yo?

00:16:43.544 --> 00:16:44.962
Is it because of the rumors?

00:16:46.422 --> 00:16:51.385
NCAPF STEERING COMMITTEE MEMBER
KANG JI-HYE

00:16:51.468 --> 00:16:53.637
This… is really strange.

00:16:57.224 --> 00:16:58.058
Or could it be

00:16:58.684 --> 00:16:59.518
a coincidence?

00:17:00.519 --> 00:17:02.521
INCOMING CALL
010-0528-8105

00:17:08.318 --> 00:17:09.153
Yes, hello?

00:17:09.737 --> 00:17:10.571
Hello Ms. Kang,

00:17:10.654 --> 00:17:13.115
my name's Choi Jeong-yo. We met the
other day.

00:17:24.376 --> 00:17:25.210
Jeong-yo.

00:17:26.336 --> 00:17:28.714
So why did you want to meet with
me here today?

00:17:29.548 --> 00:17:31.008
Is it something confidential?

00:17:32.051 --> 00:17:33.135
Oh… definitely not.

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:37.598
I'm just a bit concerned that the Hankook
Symphony Orchestra might be

00:17:37.681 --> 00:17:39.308
at a disadvantage because of me.

00:17:39.933 --> 00:17:40.768
I will show

00:17:41.560 --> 00:17:43.687
what I'm capable of. You'll see.

00:17:44.188 --> 00:17:46.065
Would you please reconsider the budget?

00:17:46.148 --> 00:17:47.066
Wow, Jeong-yo,

00:17:47.149 --> 00:17:48.650
you're just so considerate.

00:17:49.193 --> 00:17:50.027
All right.

00:17:50.694 --> 00:17:53.489
I'll move on this right now and they'll
take another look.

00:17:53.572 --> 00:17:54.990
-Hmm…
-Thank you.

00:18:02.164 --> 00:18:04.500
Jeong-yo, regarding your memory loss…

00:18:05.125 --> 00:18:08.003
How are you doing? Is there a lot you
have forgotten about?

00:18:08.087 --> 00:18:11.381
Is it just the time around the accident
that you can't recall?

00:18:12.007 --> 00:18:13.967
Or do you not remember your
childhood as well?

00:18:14.051 --> 00:18:16.386
I don't remember anything before
the accident.

00:18:17.179 --> 00:18:18.013
So…

00:18:19.431 --> 00:18:22.392
all the things that you went through
with Pi-o in school…

00:18:22.476 --> 00:18:24.478
what happened during the competition…

00:18:25.437 --> 00:18:27.981
So you don't even remember your parents,
do you?

00:18:28.732 --> 00:18:29.566
No.

00:18:32.027 --> 00:18:32.861
But you've seen

00:18:33.946 --> 00:18:35.072
a doctor, haven't you?

00:18:35.155 --> 00:18:38.367
Did they tell you anything about bringing
your memory back?

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:40.285
They said it's nearly impossible.

00:18:40.369 --> 00:18:41.411
They said that?

00:18:41.495 --> 00:18:43.247
Not even with some kind of trigger?

00:18:48.627 --> 00:18:49.586
By any chance,

00:18:50.295 --> 00:18:53.215
is there anything about my parents
that you could tell me?

00:18:54.466 --> 00:18:56.802
If you know anything at all, I'd love to
know.

00:18:57.469 --> 00:18:58.428
Anything, really.

00:18:59.429 --> 00:19:01.515
Your mom died… you were…

00:19:02.266 --> 00:19:03.142
ten years old.

00:19:03.684 --> 00:19:06.520
She died of a brain hemorrhage right in
the concert hall

00:19:06.603 --> 00:19:08.188
where you had competed earlier.

00:19:10.315 --> 00:19:12.943
I was the one who called emergency
services for her.

00:19:13.902 --> 00:19:16.155
So you can imagine how much I care about
you.

00:19:33.172 --> 00:19:34.256
Oh, I'm so sorry, ma'am.

00:19:34.339 --> 00:19:35.174
N

00:19:36.675 --> 00:19:37.634
Thank you for this.

00:19:38.218 --> 00:19:39.052
That means

00:19:39.887 --> 00:19:41.138
that I was not abandoned…

00:19:42.639 --> 00:19:44.600
or despised by my parents, after all.

00:19:46.476 --> 00:19:47.311
You know, that…

00:19:48.687 --> 00:19:50.772
That was what I actually feared the most.

00:19:52.524 --> 00:19:53.358
N

00:19:56.111 --> 00:19:58.280
Do you mind if I ask you
one more question?

00:19:59.573 --> 00:20:01.366
Are you also against Mr. Pi-o and me

00:20:01.450 --> 00:20:03.452
performing a concerto together?

00:20:04.953 --> 00:20:05.787
Oh…

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:08.665
It's not that I'm against it.

00:20:08.749 --> 00:20:10.083
But what if pushing him

00:20:10.167 --> 00:20:11.710
back onto the stage now

00:20:11.793 --> 00:20:13.962
only ends up making things worse for him.

00:20:14.838 --> 00:20:15.714
Tell me

00:20:16.215 --> 00:20:18.550
what's your reason?
This is your big debut…

00:20:19.885 --> 00:20:21.261
I'm sure it's incredibly important.

00:20:21.345 --> 00:20:22.221
So why choose Pi-o?

00:20:22.304 --> 00:20:23.889
That is the reason I chose him.

00:20:24.973 --> 00:20:26.600
It's a really big moment for me.

00:20:27.851 --> 00:20:29.937
I watched a video of your son performing.

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:31.104
And I loved it.

00:20:31.772 --> 00:20:33.899
A pianist of his caliber
on stage with me…

00:20:35.150 --> 00:20:37.027
would be an absolute dream come true.

00:20:38.528 --> 00:20:39.988
It felt like I had discovered

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.491
a rare treasure that's hard to find.

00:20:43.533 --> 00:20:46.870
From what I know, this slump started
after a mistake at a recital.

00:20:47.454 --> 00:20:50.374
It's nearly impossible to overcome
the yips, like that, with a solo

00:20:50.457 --> 00:20:51.291
performance.

00:20:51.375 --> 00:20:54.753
But in a concerto, there's someone
there to support him through it.

00:20:55.545 --> 00:20:57.881
If possible, would you mind speaking to
your son

00:20:57.965 --> 00:20:58.924
just one last time.

00:20:59.591 --> 00:21:00.425
I'm…

00:21:01.260 --> 00:21:04.012
confident I can help Pi-o overcome
this slump for good.

00:21:08.767 --> 00:21:10.602
I'm glad we had the chance to do this.

00:21:10.686 --> 00:21:12.354
Let's do this again sometime.

00:21:12.437 --> 00:21:14.690
-Thank you for your time.
-Have a good night.

00:21:15.315 --> 00:21:16.149
You too.

00:21:30.289 --> 00:21:32.416
Pi-o, it's mom.

00:21:33.417 --> 00:21:34.251
Can I come in?

00:21:35.627 --> 00:21:36.503
Go ahead.

00:21:48.056 --> 00:21:49.474
How are you doing, honey?

00:21:49.558 --> 00:21:51.393
Is there something you want from me?

00:21:52.060 --> 00:21:52.936
It's just that I…

00:21:55.105 --> 00:21:56.690
met with Jeong-yo earlier.

00:21:59.234 --> 00:22:00.402
Oh… but what for?

00:22:00.902 --> 00:22:04.573
He really wants to perform a concerto
with you. And asked me to convince you.

00:22:04.656 --> 00:22:05.991
He said he was captivated

00:22:06.491 --> 00:22:09.328
by your playing after watching a video of
your performance.

00:22:09.411 --> 00:22:11.538
He doesn't want the world ending up
without your music.

00:22:11.621 --> 00:22:13.874
It's… really moving isn't it?

00:22:15.792 --> 00:22:16.793
I'm very aware…

00:22:17.586 --> 00:22:19.921
that you have conflicting feelings
about him.

00:22:20.005 --> 00:22:21.923
But I think this might actually be

00:22:22.007 --> 00:22:23.800
a good opportunity and it's worth a try.

00:22:23.884 --> 00:22:27.220
At the end of the day, a concerto is less
stressful than a solo recital,

00:22:27.304 --> 00:22:28.430
and if you think about it,

00:22:28.513 --> 00:22:30.724
you and Jeong-yo had really great
chemistry.

00:22:31.391 --> 00:22:33.393
Mom, are you trying to tell me
what to do?

00:22:33.477 --> 00:22:36.188
I won't force you if you really
don't want to do it, but I'd like you

00:22:36.271 --> 00:22:37.981
to give it some thought, will you?

00:22:38.982 --> 00:22:41.193
Well, all I can do is give you my two
cents.

00:22:41.902 --> 00:22:43.904
At the end of the day, it's your choice.

00:22:55.290 --> 00:22:56.708
MARTIN VOGEL

00:22:57.209 --> 00:22:58.752
How long is this gonna take?

00:22:59.252 --> 00:23:01.922
I think it'll take some time. You have
to be patient.

00:23:02.881 --> 00:23:04.383
JAE-IN

00:23:04.466 --> 00:23:07.427
You know Hye-jeong's piano trio
concert is coming up, right?

00:23:07.511 --> 00:23:08.345
Pi-yo,

00:23:08.428 --> 00:23:09.262
Wanna go see it?

00:23:20.482 --> 00:23:21.316
Oh!

00:23:28.031 --> 00:23:28.865
There you are.

00:23:32.327 --> 00:23:33.161
Oh…

00:23:33.745 --> 00:23:36.415
Hye-jeong
invited Jeong-yo to the performance.

00:24:17.622 --> 00:24:19.541
My dear… you came.

00:24:19.624 --> 00:24:22.043
-Thank you for showing up.
-Don't mention it.

00:24:23.211 --> 00:24:25.964
I came because I haven't seen a
performance in a while.

00:24:26.047 --> 00:24:26.882
Oh, yeah?

00:24:27.549 --> 00:24:29.134
When would you have come

00:24:29.217 --> 00:24:31.761
to see a performance with Yoon Han-rim
in it?

00:24:32.637 --> 00:24:33.638
Come on, admit it,

00:24:33.722 --> 00:24:35.474
you came for my sake, didn't you?

00:24:40.896 --> 00:24:42.522
Hm! Jeong-yo.

00:24:43.815 --> 00:24:44.649
Hey.

00:24:47.861 --> 00:24:49.029
How was the performance?

00:24:49.112 --> 00:24:51.323
-Was it any good?
-It was nice.

00:24:51.406 --> 00:24:53.200
-Yeah.
-I liked all three of them.

00:24:53.700 --> 00:24:55.076
The ensemble was good too.

00:24:55.160 --> 00:24:57.704
All three of them are from our alma mater.

00:24:58.497 --> 00:25:00.499
They're all music majors from our grade.

00:25:01.124 --> 00:25:01.958
Ah.

00:25:02.501 --> 00:25:03.376
But who was…

00:25:04.252 --> 00:25:06.004
the one playing the piano just now?

00:25:07.005 --> 00:25:08.465
I thought he was really good.

00:25:09.799 --> 00:25:10.926
Hmm. Good in what way?

00:25:12.302 --> 00:25:13.803
I thought he was forcing it.

00:25:14.596 --> 00:25:15.430
Really?

00:25:16.139 --> 00:25:18.183
Jeong-yo! Jeong-yo!

00:25:18.266 --> 00:25:21.228
Hey, Jeong-yo! Whoa! Hey! Oh, look at you.

00:25:22.020 --> 00:25:22.854
Man…

00:25:22.938 --> 00:25:26.566
you know how worried sick all of our
classmates were when you disappeared?

00:25:26.650 --> 00:25:27.734
I forgot…

00:25:27.817 --> 00:25:29.694
you have no memories from back then.

00:25:29.778 --> 00:25:30.737
Oh.

00:25:30.820 --> 00:25:34.616
For sure you don't remember that you
and me used fight all the time in school.

00:25:34.699 --> 00:25:35.534
I used to fight?

00:25:35.617 --> 00:25:36.451
Oh, yeah!

00:25:36.535 --> 00:25:40.205
I mean, we were just teenagers full of
adrenaline and hormones back then,

00:25:40.288 --> 00:25:42.374
we were just young, so we fought a lot.

00:25:42.457 --> 00:25:46.127
It's okay, man. Kids become friends by
fighting and stuff, you know that.

00:25:47.504 --> 00:25:49.297
Oh, dude…

00:25:49.381 --> 00:25:52.259
I heard you joined the Hankook Symphony
Orchestra as a conductor.

00:25:52.342 --> 00:25:55.220
-I start early next month.
-Oh… who are you performing with?

00:25:55.303 --> 00:25:56.763
I still haven't decided.

00:25:57.764 --> 00:25:59.516
Well… Then how about me?

00:26:00.016 --> 00:26:03.436
I'd much rather play in a big stage
that in a tiny venue like this.

00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:05.063
Man… I'll be open with you.

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.274
I was deeply moved by you

00:26:07.357 --> 00:26:09.401
when I saw you conduct for the
first time.

00:26:09.484 --> 00:26:10.485
Hmm,

00:26:10.569 --> 00:26:13.738
to be perfectly honest, I think we could
make great music together.

00:26:13.822 --> 00:26:15.490
I think we should join forces.

00:26:16.616 --> 00:26:18.076
Okay, I'll think about it.

00:26:18.159 --> 00:26:19.286
Great, thanks, man.

00:26:20.579 --> 00:26:22.622
Hey, Jeong-yo, about the soloist…

00:26:22.706 --> 00:26:24.291
we should discuss it a bit more--

00:26:24.374 --> 00:26:25.250
Hey, Hong Jae-in.

00:26:26.042 --> 00:26:28.336
Trying to interfere
with my sales pitch again?

00:26:28.420 --> 00:26:29.379
Huh?

00:26:29.462 --> 00:26:33.300
If the pianist and the conductor
are on the same page, then that's that.

00:26:35.218 --> 00:26:36.803
Hey, ladies… coming for drinks?

00:26:36.886 --> 00:26:38.888
-Okay, but just a few.
-Fine, we'll be there.

00:26:38.972 --> 00:26:41.266
All right then, it's at Luce Beers.
Join us there later. You better come,

00:26:41.349 --> 00:26:42.183
okay?

00:26:43.101 --> 00:26:45.562
I booked us
some tables at Luce Beers for a nightcap.

00:26:45.645 --> 00:26:46.605
Don't go home just yet.

00:26:46.688 --> 00:26:48.523
Come for a drink and we can go over it

00:26:48.607 --> 00:26:50.400
a little bit more. Are you coming?

00:26:50.483 --> 00:26:51.443
Sure.

00:26:51.526 --> 00:26:54.779
Great. See you in a bit. Yeah. Ha…

00:26:55.947 --> 00:26:58.158
All of you better be there! I'll be
waiting.

00:26:58.241 --> 00:26:59.909
-Of course! We'll be there.
-We're coming! See you in a bit.

00:26:59.993 --> 00:27:02.370
Are you really considering
performing with him?

00:27:02.912 --> 00:27:06.333
Listen, I know it's not my place to say
this, but he's not your guy.

00:27:07.709 --> 00:27:10.211
His music lacks soul and honestly,
so does he.

00:27:10.295 --> 00:27:13.965
Do you really want someone like that
to perform with you for your debut?

00:27:14.049 --> 00:27:16.426
I think you should reconsider
your choice.

00:27:16.509 --> 00:27:17.636
Is that so?

00:27:18.386 --> 00:27:21.598
Then why don't you do the concerto
with me, so I don't have to perform

00:27:21.681 --> 00:27:22.641
with him?

00:27:23.892 --> 00:27:26.269
I would much rather perform with you,
Mr. Pi-o.

00:27:27.270 --> 00:27:29.189
I watched a video of your performance,

00:27:29.856 --> 00:27:31.107
and it was spectacular.

00:27:32.275 --> 00:27:33.735
And I'm asking you to do this

00:27:34.736 --> 00:27:37.405
because performing with you would make
me look good.

00:27:39.449 --> 00:27:40.700
What do you mean by that?

00:27:41.242 --> 00:27:44.579
The Hankook Symphony Orchestra is
notorious for being territorial.

00:27:45.288 --> 00:27:47.123
Since I was brought in unexpectedly,

00:27:48.416 --> 00:27:50.877
I still have a lot to do to prove
myself to them.

00:27:52.712 --> 00:27:55.382
If you do this, it would really
help me out big time.

00:27:56.049 --> 00:27:58.551
I understand what you're saying, but the
thing is,

00:27:59.135 --> 00:28:01.680
I still haven't gotten over my slump,
I told you--

00:28:01.763 --> 00:28:04.599
It's just something you'll have to face
sooner or later.

00:28:06.851 --> 00:28:07.686
Mr. Pi-o.

00:28:11.439 --> 00:28:13.024
I think it will be really good.

00:28:16.444 --> 00:28:17.278
N

00:28:22.075 --> 00:28:24.494
I would much rather perform with you,
Mr. Pi-o.

00:28:28.581 --> 00:28:31.251
If you do this, it would really
help me out big time.

00:28:32.210 --> 00:28:35.046
It's just something you'll have to face
sooner or later.

00:28:51.062 --> 00:28:52.939
KANG PI-O

00:28:53.022 --> 00:28:54.190
I'm in. Let's do it.

00:29:00.697 --> 00:29:02.907
In the end, I guess you got
what you wanted.

00:29:03.992 --> 00:29:06.077
I told you this was risky, but you don't
listen.

00:29:06.161 --> 00:29:08.705
With all due respect, I don't think
it'll be risky.

00:29:08.788 --> 00:29:10.373
I whole-heartedly believe that

00:29:10.999 --> 00:29:13.835
Mr. Kang-Pio is the best partner for a
successful debut.

00:29:15.128 --> 00:29:15.962
What about the program?

00:29:16.045 --> 00:29:16.880
Hm?

00:29:16.963 --> 00:29:20.425
You said the second half would be
Brahms One, the piece that won you the

00:29:20.508 --> 00:29:21.676
conducting competition.

00:29:22.343 --> 00:29:23.303
And the first half?

00:29:23.845 --> 00:29:26.181
Have the two of you already
agreed on that?

00:29:26.264 --> 00:29:28.433
Um… actually, we haven't yet…

00:29:30.852 --> 00:29:32.103
What do you want to play?

00:29:32.687 --> 00:29:34.022
Have you thought about it?

00:29:36.024 --> 00:29:38.234
Ravel. That's what I would like to play.

00:29:38.735 --> 00:29:41.237
No, that would just muddy the theme.

00:29:43.531 --> 00:29:46.326
How about Mozart's Piano Concerto Twenty
instead?

00:29:47.368 --> 00:29:48.953
From a storytelling standpoint,

00:29:49.037 --> 00:29:52.123
it shows you coming out of the darkness
and into the light.

00:29:52.207 --> 00:29:55.502
So pairing Mozart Twenty and Brahms
One would actually keep

00:29:56.085 --> 00:29:59.005
-the overall program more cohesive.
-But think about it,

00:29:59.798 --> 00:30:02.926
Pi-o has never played Mozart Twenty
before, and as you know,

00:30:03.009 --> 00:30:04.552
it is not exactly an easy piece--

00:30:04.636 --> 00:30:05.720
What are you saying?

00:30:06.721 --> 00:30:09.682
Are professionals only supposed to
play what they already know?

00:30:09.766 --> 00:30:10.809
Hm.

00:30:10.892 --> 00:30:11.810
Well,

00:30:11.893 --> 00:30:14.771
if you feel, like we might be pushing it,
I don't mind performing something

00:30:14.854 --> 00:30:15.688
-you've--
-No.

00:30:16.856 --> 00:30:17.857
I know I can do it.

00:30:19.818 --> 00:30:20.652
I will do it.

00:30:21.277 --> 00:30:22.111
N

00:30:22.821 --> 00:30:24.489
ENSEMBLE ROOM

00:30:26.157 --> 00:30:27.534
Are you sure you can do it?

00:30:29.994 --> 00:30:31.621
Because if you think it might be too
much--

00:30:31.704 --> 00:30:32.956
Do you think it's too much?

00:30:33.039 --> 00:30:34.290
I told you I could do it.

00:30:43.883 --> 00:30:46.427
What made you think this would be a good
idea?

00:30:46.511 --> 00:30:49.514
He was so adamant about it that I finally
gave in. But if he ends up ruining

00:30:49.597 --> 00:30:50.807
his debut because of this--

00:30:50.890 --> 00:30:54.394
What do you think is unique about
Choi Jeong-yo's way of doing things?

00:30:55.019 --> 00:30:57.897
It's the audacity to do the impossible.
That's his charm.

00:30:58.731 --> 00:30:59.816
And the sheer ferocity

00:30:59.899 --> 00:31:01.860
with which he manages to pull it off.

00:31:02.652 --> 00:31:03.570
And if he doesn't?

00:31:05.572 --> 00:31:07.490
We'll deal with the aftermath of that.

00:31:11.244 --> 00:31:13.204
The orchestra's eightieth is coming up.

00:31:15.331 --> 00:31:18.293
It's now time that a new conductor
showed up and took over.

00:31:19.043 --> 00:31:20.169
So we should use this

00:31:22.171 --> 00:31:25.508
as a chance to see whether Choi Jeong-yo
is capable of doing that.

00:32:32.533 --> 00:32:33.451
Excuse me…

00:32:34.994 --> 00:32:36.996
I reserved a practice room.

00:32:38.706 --> 00:32:39.540
Uh…

00:32:41.292 --> 00:32:44.003
-You can go to Room Three if you'd like.
-Thanks.

00:32:53.429 --> 00:32:54.263
Hey.

00:32:55.181 --> 00:32:57.350
Do you know who just came
to practice here?

00:32:58.768 --> 00:32:59.811
Kang Pi-o himself!

00:33:13.783 --> 00:33:15.743
-What?
-This is insane!

00:33:16.327 --> 00:33:18.454
Guess what Kang Pi-o is playing
right now.

00:33:19.038 --> 00:33:20.206
He's playing Hanon One.

00:33:21.207 --> 00:33:23.584
HEY, THIS IS INSANE
GUESS WHAT KANG PI-O IS PLAYING RIGHT NOW

00:33:23.668 --> 00:33:26.129
HAHAHAHAHA
IS KANG PI-O AN ELEMENTARY SCHOOL KID?

00:35:54.193 --> 00:35:55.862
What brings you all the way here?

00:36:02.243 --> 00:36:03.077
Choi Jeong-yo.

00:36:04.370 --> 00:36:05.329
I'm really sorry,

00:36:06.080 --> 00:36:07.248
but I need your help.

00:36:09.041 --> 00:36:10.293
I've been trying to overcome it,

00:36:10.376 --> 00:36:11.210
but I can't.

00:36:12.962 --> 00:36:15.173
I don't know how, but I memorized
the piece,

00:36:15.756 --> 00:36:18.217
but I'm still completely terrified
of having to perform

00:36:18.301 --> 00:36:19.510
in front of people.

00:36:20.094 --> 00:36:22.805
And I… don't have the slightest idea

00:36:24.473 --> 00:36:25.474
how to overcome it.

00:36:26.851 --> 00:36:28.728
I don't care if I ruin my reputation,

00:36:29.228 --> 00:36:31.147
but I won't drag you down with me.

00:36:32.523 --> 00:36:34.483
If you decide I won't be able to do it,

00:36:36.152 --> 00:36:37.069
find someone else.

00:36:41.866 --> 00:36:43.743
Do you have some free time right now?

00:36:44.285 --> 00:36:45.745
I want to take you somewhere.

00:37:10.728 --> 00:37:13.648
I just happened to hear him
playing one day on the subway.

00:37:14.774 --> 00:37:17.360
He usually out here around this time
on the weekends.

00:37:17.443 --> 00:37:18.486
Isn't it something?

00:37:19.153 --> 00:37:21.239
To hear a performance like this out here?

00:37:22.949 --> 00:37:25.701
Mr. Pi-o, why do you think people even
listen to music?

00:37:28.704 --> 00:37:31.791
Because it offers us some comfort in
the crazy chaos of life.

00:37:32.750 --> 00:37:36.212
And do you think the people listening
to this music right now

00:37:36.295 --> 00:37:38.506
are standing here judging him by any
chance?

00:37:39.257 --> 00:37:40.091
They're not.

00:37:41.300 --> 00:37:43.052
They're all being comforted by him.

00:37:44.428 --> 00:37:46.555
But what I need you to look at closely
now

00:37:47.640 --> 00:37:49.141
is the expression on his face.

00:37:49.767 --> 00:37:50.643
Does he look like

00:37:51.143 --> 00:37:53.396
he's afraid of being judged by the
audience?

00:37:53.479 --> 00:37:54.647
He does not.

00:37:55.648 --> 00:37:56.482
Not at all.

00:37:57.275 --> 00:37:58.109
The thing is…

00:37:58.192 --> 00:38:01.279
he's finding joy in the very music
he's playing.

00:38:01.362 --> 00:38:02.530
Because he's the one

00:38:03.030 --> 00:38:05.366
being comforted by his music more than
anyone.

00:38:07.034 --> 00:38:07.868
Has something

00:38:08.828 --> 00:38:11.038
happened recently that's been bothering
you?

00:38:13.291 --> 00:38:16.919
Maybe… something broke inside you
and your slump might've started there.

00:38:18.212 --> 00:38:21.048
I'm sure you know that before playing
for anyone else, you have to play for

00:38:21.132 --> 00:38:21.966
yourself.

00:38:22.508 --> 00:38:24.802
Before you can even think of comforting
anyone,

00:38:24.885 --> 00:38:26.053
you need to figure out how

00:38:26.137 --> 00:38:27.013
to soothe your own…

00:38:27.096 --> 00:38:28.472
wounds and heal your heart.

00:38:29.849 --> 00:38:30.683
To start out,

00:38:31.225 --> 00:38:34.020
try playing music for yourself,
to comfort your heart.

00:38:58.169 --> 00:38:59.170
Tell me the truth.

00:38:59.712 --> 00:39:01.047
Just tell me who his father is.

00:39:01.130 --> 00:39:02.840
And send him back to that bastard!

00:39:02.923 --> 00:39:05.468
I've told you already, why don't you
believe me.

00:39:05.551 --> 00:39:06.802
He doesn't have a father.

00:39:07.303 --> 00:39:08.262
Pi-o is

00:39:08.763 --> 00:39:10.931
a gift sent to me by God. He's a miracle.

00:39:11.015 --> 00:39:13.184
Oh, my goodness, you've lost your mind.

00:39:13.684 --> 00:39:14.518
You're insane!

00:39:15.186 --> 00:39:16.687
You have gone completely mad!

00:39:26.530 --> 00:39:27.365
N

00:39:43.130 --> 00:39:46.759
Maybe… something broke inside you
and your slump might've started there.

00:39:47.551 --> 00:39:51.347
Mr. Kang Pi-o, have you ever… just played
music to comfort your own heart?

00:40:31.470 --> 00:40:34.306
I'm sure you know that before playing for
anyone else, you have to play for

00:40:34.390 --> 00:40:35.224
yourself.

00:40:35.307 --> 00:40:37.685
Before you can even think of comforting
anyone,

00:40:37.768 --> 00:40:40.438
you need to figure out how to soothe
your own wounds…

00:42:01.769 --> 00:42:03.896
You're all checked in. Have a good
evening.

00:42:03.979 --> 00:42:06.273
2026 KOREA LUCENA GRAND AWARDS

00:42:06.357 --> 00:42:07.191
That's great!

00:42:08.651 --> 00:42:10.361
-Good to see you.
-Oh, hi!

00:42:11.070 --> 00:42:13.072
-It's been forever.
-Yeah, way too long.

00:42:14.573 --> 00:42:16.242
-Where's your seat?
-I'll pin it on you.

00:42:16.325 --> 00:42:17.159
It's further up.

00:42:18.661 --> 00:42:20.788
I'll see you later then. I will, won't I?

00:42:26.335 --> 00:42:28.128
-Oh, hello sir.
-Ah, yes, hello.

00:42:28.212 --> 00:42:29.088
How have you been?

00:42:29.171 --> 00:42:31.590
-Oh, hello.
-How long has it been since the last time?

00:42:31.674 --> 00:42:32.508
Ah…

00:42:32.591 --> 00:42:34.969
-It feels like just the other day. Yes.
-I know, right?

00:42:35.469 --> 00:42:36.720
You're doing well, I hope?

00:42:36.804 --> 00:42:38.931
Jeong-yo, nice to see you here.

00:42:39.014 --> 00:42:41.600
-It's a pleasure to see you.
-Oh. Hello Ms. Kang.

00:42:41.684 --> 00:42:43.769
-Hello.
-Gosh, Ms. Yoon.

00:42:43.852 --> 00:42:45.646
You should have told me in advance

00:42:45.729 --> 00:42:48.107
that you were going to bring Jeong-yo
with you.

00:42:49.358 --> 00:42:51.360
Since you could not provide the subsidy,

00:42:52.027 --> 00:42:54.572
what choice did I have but to send
the man of the hour in search for

00:42:54.655 --> 00:42:56.699
sponsors?
Though it's hardly a musician's job.

00:42:56.782 --> 00:42:59.868
If you put it like that, Jeong-yo might
misunderstand you.

00:42:59.952 --> 00:43:02.746
I've been working myself to the bone
for the Hankook Symphony Orchestra

00:43:02.830 --> 00:43:04.498
-lately.
-Ms. Yoon.

00:43:04.582 --> 00:43:06.667
Oh, my. Hello, director!

00:43:08.502 --> 00:43:09.545
When did you get here?

00:43:09.628 --> 00:43:11.797
-Just a moment ago…
-What on earth did you do?

00:43:11.880 --> 00:43:13.882
His playing sounds completely different
now.

00:43:13.966 --> 00:43:15.968
He's just been playing nonstop as of
late,

00:43:16.051 --> 00:43:17.678
but something's different now.

00:43:17.761 --> 00:43:19.680
I can feel the joy in his music.

00:43:19.763 --> 00:43:20.973
What have you done?

00:43:22.349 --> 00:43:24.518
That's Pi-o's hard work finally
paying off.

00:43:26.770 --> 00:43:28.314
Sure… did you see what I sent you?

00:43:28.397 --> 00:43:29.231
Oh, yes I did.

00:43:33.235 --> 00:43:35.195
Distinguished guests, honored attendees,

00:43:35.279 --> 00:43:38.115
and the award winners who are the
stars of this event.

00:43:38.949 --> 00:43:41.827
It is a great honor to deliver this
congratulatory address at such a

00:43:41.910 --> 00:43:43.162
meaningful event.

00:43:43.245 --> 00:43:44.079
The name Lucena

00:43:44.163 --> 00:43:47.833
means "a shining companion of the arts,
even in the darkest of times"

00:43:48.500 --> 00:43:52.046
Art is a delicate flower that always
blooms from the deepest parts of the

00:43:52.129 --> 00:43:52.963
human soul.

00:43:53.047 --> 00:43:55.674
-However, for that flower to fully
-Excuse me for a second.

00:43:55.758 --> 00:43:57.843
Bloom in society,
it will definitely need

00:43:57.926 --> 00:43:59.887
-Hm-hmm.
-someone's care and attention.

00:44:07.561 --> 00:44:09.772
He's just been playing nonstop
as of late,

00:44:09.855 --> 00:44:11.398
but something's different now.

00:44:11.482 --> 00:44:13.317
I can feel the joy in his music.

00:44:13.400 --> 00:44:14.652
What have you done?

00:44:31.126 --> 00:44:33.128
Let's just play again. What do you think?

00:44:33.212 --> 00:44:34.254
Okay.

00:44:35.172 --> 00:44:37.132
Hey, don't be sore if I beat you, okay?

00:44:37.758 --> 00:44:39.218
When we play, let's have fun!

00:44:40.344 --> 00:44:42.346
Oh, please. I'm the one who's gonna win.

00:44:42.888 --> 00:44:44.056
So you can't get upset.

00:44:47.643 --> 00:44:49.478
PERFORMERS' GREEN ROOM
THIS WAY

00:45:15.045 --> 00:45:17.339
Let's be real, I'm clearly
in first place.

00:45:17.423 --> 00:45:18.549
You know it.

00:45:19.341 --> 00:45:21.385
-Hmm…
-Hey.

00:45:21.468 --> 00:45:23.011
-You wish.
-I'm gonna win.

00:45:51.915 --> 00:45:52.750
Jeong-yo.

00:45:54.084 --> 00:45:55.294
What are you doing here?

00:45:56.795 --> 00:45:57.629
Oh, I…

00:45:59.381 --> 00:46:01.842
I went to the restroom and couldn't
find my way back.

00:46:01.925 --> 00:46:05.220
Then I happened to spot the piano,
so I just came in to see it.

00:46:05.804 --> 00:46:06.638
It's like

00:46:08.140 --> 00:46:09.308
it's somewhat familiar.

00:46:10.350 --> 00:46:12.561
This place hasn't changed
much since then.

00:46:13.103 --> 00:46:13.937
Is there

00:46:14.897 --> 00:46:16.106
anything you remembered?

00:46:17.691 --> 00:46:18.525
No.

00:46:19.443 --> 00:46:20.277
Why?

00:46:21.820 --> 00:46:22.654
Nothing…

00:46:24.907 --> 00:46:25.741
Shall we go?

00:46:56.021 --> 00:46:56.855
Hey, Pi-o.

00:46:59.566 --> 00:47:00.400
How've you been?

00:47:03.904 --> 00:47:04.905
You haven't changed.

00:47:06.865 --> 00:47:09.827
Man, Han-rim and I were completely shocked

00:47:10.661 --> 00:47:12.079
you were doing the concerto.

00:47:13.330 --> 00:47:14.790
What's that supposed to mean?

00:47:17.417 --> 00:47:18.252
You know…

00:47:19.545 --> 00:47:20.379
there…

00:47:20.879 --> 00:47:23.966
were these rumors going around that you
were involved with Choi Jeong-yo's

00:47:24.049 --> 00:47:25.175
disappearance somehow.

00:47:26.343 --> 00:47:27.553
So when we heard you were

00:47:27.636 --> 00:47:28.637
here

00:47:28.720 --> 00:47:29.972
we were like, "Huh?

00:47:30.055 --> 00:47:31.139
That's so weird.”

00:47:32.182 --> 00:47:33.642
Who the hell's saying that crap?

00:47:33.725 --> 00:47:35.769
Whoa. So scary…

00:47:36.603 --> 00:47:38.021
If you were not, then great.

00:47:38.897 --> 00:47:40.649
Oh, my, what vulgar language

00:47:41.233 --> 00:47:42.818
from someone so classy.

00:47:44.653 --> 00:47:45.571
At rehearsal today

00:47:46.530 --> 00:47:47.614
try… not to mess up.

00:47:50.200 --> 00:47:51.159
Good luck.

00:48:06.592 --> 00:48:07.467
Wow, look at him.

00:48:08.802 --> 00:48:09.636
Unbelievable.

00:48:10.304 --> 00:48:13.056
-Is he okay? He doesn't look good.
-He doesn't seem confident.

00:48:13.140 --> 00:48:15.559
-What's his problem?
-I mean, you've heard about it, right?

00:48:15.642 --> 00:48:17.895
-He shouldn't be here.
-Can he even play now?

00:48:19.813 --> 00:48:21.773
It's the worst possible thing really.

00:48:21.857 --> 00:48:24.151
Gosh, you know what, I jut really
don't get it.

00:48:24.234 --> 00:48:27.112
I mean, I get that he's Kang Pi-o
and all that, but why would anyone book

00:48:27.195 --> 00:48:28.655
a soloist who's in a slump?

00:48:29.489 --> 00:48:31.325
-Exactly.
-I know, right?

00:48:31.408 --> 00:48:33.118
Well, his family's rich, you know?

00:48:33.702 --> 00:48:35.370
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:48:35.454 --> 00:48:36.288
-Hello.
-Hello.

00:48:36.371 --> 00:48:37.205
Hello.

00:49:33.053 --> 00:49:34.554
Cellos, you're slightly ahead.

00:49:35.180 --> 00:49:37.891
Make sure you come in right on
the piano's final note.

00:49:38.433 --> 00:49:39.267
Okay.

00:49:40.143 --> 00:49:42.729
The piano's all over the place.
What do we do then?

00:49:45.732 --> 00:49:46.650
Pianist Kang Pi-o.

00:49:47.943 --> 00:49:51.196
At the cutoff, make sure the next
downbeat lands exactly on time.

00:49:53.907 --> 00:49:54.741
Understood.

00:49:55.492 --> 00:49:56.326
Again.

00:49:56.868 --> 00:49:58.286
Start from the piano solo.

00:49:58.370 --> 00:49:59.329
N

00:50:17.681 --> 00:50:19.641
I mean, it's not like he's bad,

00:50:19.725 --> 00:50:21.685
but doesn't he feel a little shaky?

00:50:22.394 --> 00:50:24.604
And he plays it differently every
single time.

00:50:24.688 --> 00:50:27.816
Maybe he's not completely out of his
slump just yet, you know?

00:50:27.899 --> 00:50:28.734
Well…

00:50:29.234 --> 00:50:30.986
There's always a period of transition.

00:50:31.069 --> 00:50:34.740
Yeah, but why do we have to bear the
brunt of his period of transition?

00:50:34.823 --> 00:50:38.118
To be honest, I just don't get it.
Choi Jeong-yo and Kang Pi-o

00:50:38.201 --> 00:50:41.413
are every bit as arrogant and
insufferable now as they were when we

00:50:41.496 --> 00:50:42.497
were back in school.

00:50:49.963 --> 00:50:51.131
Why are you still here?

00:50:51.965 --> 00:50:53.675
Rehearsal ended quite a while ago.

00:50:54.968 --> 00:50:55.802
Hey.

00:51:01.099 --> 00:51:03.101
Why did you ask me to perform with you?

00:51:07.814 --> 00:51:09.191
It feels like everyone…

00:51:10.567 --> 00:51:13.195
is waiting for me to crash and burn
whenever I play.

00:51:15.739 --> 00:51:18.366
Holding on to my confidence is getting
harder to do.

00:51:20.744 --> 00:51:21.745
So what made you…

00:51:25.707 --> 00:51:27.584
believe I'd be able to pull this off?

00:51:29.419 --> 00:51:30.337
N

00:51:37.844 --> 00:51:38.678
Hm…

00:51:40.305 --> 00:51:41.139
I don't know.

00:51:43.100 --> 00:51:46.603
But I think they might be acting that way
because they're reacting more to me

00:51:46.686 --> 00:51:47.521
than to you.

00:51:49.147 --> 00:51:52.317
It seems to me, that we have no one
but each other to count on.

00:51:54.861 --> 00:51:55.695
N

00:51:57.489 --> 00:51:58.907
When I was at the monastery,

00:52:01.159 --> 00:52:03.286
I had a really bad case of
social anxiety.

00:52:04.454 --> 00:52:08.083
I could barely be around people, but I
so desperately wanted to play music.

00:52:08.166 --> 00:52:09.209
N

00:52:10.627 --> 00:52:11.461
So I created

00:52:12.212 --> 00:52:14.756
an orchestra that only existed in my
imagination.

00:52:16.424 --> 00:52:19.261
I had conversations with them. I even
argued with them.

00:52:22.305 --> 00:52:24.141
As it turned out… N

00:52:24.808 --> 00:52:27.435
That was the greatest weapon a conductor
could have.

00:52:28.395 --> 00:52:30.355
And that's because any good conductor…

00:52:32.023 --> 00:52:34.943
needs to have everything figured out
way before stepping in front of the

00:52:35.026 --> 00:52:35.861
orchestra.

00:52:41.908 --> 00:52:43.743
Mr. Pi-o, if fear keeps creeping in,

00:52:44.828 --> 00:52:46.788
map it all out in your head, in detail.

00:52:48.331 --> 00:52:49.291
Then at some point,

00:52:50.500 --> 00:52:53.128
this fear you're feeling, will completely
fade away.

00:52:54.171 --> 00:52:55.255
I know it's not easy,

00:52:57.090 --> 00:52:59.050
but you'll have to trust me implicitly.

00:52:59.885 --> 00:53:02.012
Because I'm the one guiding the
orchestra.

00:53:03.138 --> 00:53:05.724
Would you like to hear the music in my
imagination?

00:53:08.101 --> 00:53:09.936
Oh, if you don't mind,

00:53:11.938 --> 00:53:13.356
a piano would be helpful.

00:53:40.842 --> 00:53:41.676
Violin.

00:53:42.677 --> 00:53:43.720
Pianissimo.

00:53:55.690 --> 00:53:56.524
Cello, bass.

00:54:06.451 --> 00:54:08.161
-Oboe, flute,
-Espressivo!

00:54:33.019 --> 00:54:34.020
Timpani, forte!

00:54:56.501 --> 00:54:57.335
Piano.

00:54:58.753 --> 00:55:00.130
Con dolore.

00:57:22.897 --> 00:57:23.773
That was amazing!

00:57:29.446 --> 00:57:30.363
How are you doing?

00:57:31.114 --> 00:57:31.948
Oh,

00:57:32.031 --> 00:57:33.658
thank you for coming out to the
performance today.

00:57:33.741 --> 00:57:34.576
Hm-hmm.

00:57:34.659 --> 00:57:37.454
I'd appreciate it if you could write an
article about it.

00:57:37.537 --> 00:57:39.414
Oh, of course! It'll be my pleasure.

00:57:39.497 --> 00:57:41.332
Yes, of course. Let's keep in touch.

00:57:43.418 --> 00:57:44.252
Hmm.

00:57:47.505 --> 00:57:48.339
Hi, I'm back.

00:57:49.466 --> 00:57:52.093
Oh, my gosh, it was so emotional.
I was literally holding back tears

00:57:52.177 --> 00:57:53.011
at the end.

00:57:53.094 --> 00:57:56.097
How do you two manage to touch my heart
every single time!

00:57:56.639 --> 00:57:58.016
I want to thank both of you

00:57:58.558 --> 00:58:00.143
for helping me all the way through.

00:58:00.226 --> 00:58:01.561
Oh, not at all.

00:58:02.520 --> 00:58:04.397
I was really scared up there tonight.

00:58:05.231 --> 00:58:08.151
But I was absolutely blown away by how
well you performed.

00:58:09.110 --> 00:58:09.944
Oh, wait!

00:58:10.028 --> 00:58:13.281
Let's do something with the two of you
for the anniversary festival.

00:58:13.364 --> 00:58:14.949
But you've gotta perform together!

00:58:15.033 --> 00:58:18.745
I wanna take this opportunity, and turn
you into a brand. What do you say?

00:58:18.828 --> 00:58:19.662
I don't know…

00:58:20.580 --> 00:58:21.414
Oh.

00:58:22.665 --> 00:58:24.209
Whoa, with all these calls…

00:58:24.292 --> 00:58:26.044
we're barely getting to talk today!

00:58:26.586 --> 00:58:27.587
Give me a sec?

00:58:30.131 --> 00:58:30.965
HI, it's Jae-in.

00:58:34.135 --> 00:58:34.969
Mr. Pi-o.

00:58:36.304 --> 00:58:37.138
Hmm?

00:58:38.556 --> 00:58:40.892
Now that our performance has ended
successfully,

00:58:40.975 --> 00:58:43.144
there's something that I'd like to say.

00:58:47.690 --> 00:58:48.525
So…

00:58:49.317 --> 00:58:50.276
By any chance--

00:58:52.737 --> 00:58:53.571
Oh…

00:58:58.701 --> 00:59:01.788
I found out who was behind the order
to kidnap Choi Jeong-yo.

00:59:05.583 --> 00:59:06.543
What is it?

00:59:07.335 --> 00:59:08.419
Did something happen?

00:59:09.462 --> 00:59:10.296
Oh… not at all.

00:59:11.881 --> 00:59:12.715
Do you mind?

01:00:32.378 --> 01:00:34.339
FOUR HANDS, TWO SONATAS

01:00:35.590 --> 01:00:36.841
Mom, why did you do it?

01:00:36.924 --> 01:00:39.510
We have to confess to Jeong-yo and beg
for forgiveness.

01:00:39.594 --> 01:00:41.387
-I won't go!
-If the truth comes out,

01:00:41.471 --> 01:00:43.890
not only will my life be over, but yours
too.

01:00:43.973 --> 01:00:45.600
Why that look on your face?

01:00:45.683 --> 01:00:47.435
Are you hiding something from me?

01:00:47.518 --> 01:00:49.771
I didn't have the courage to tell the
truth back then.

01:00:49.854 --> 01:00:51.064
What if he's up to something?

01:00:51.147 --> 01:00:55.193
I'm worried out of my mind that you keep
getting mixed up with him at every turn.

01:00:55.276 --> 01:00:56.861
I'm sure he's hiding something.

01:00:58.738 --> 01:01:00.782
At the Hermione International
Competition…